f}
\begin{remark}
This rule prevents reporting from a \emph{detected} inconsistent
context. It cannot guarantee detection of every inconsistency, and
finite inability to prove consistency is not proof of inconsistency.
\end{remark}

\section{Finite Ocean suites and universal claims}
\begin{proposition}[Finite-test nonuniversality]
Passing a finite set $O$ of sampled tests for a property over an
infinite domain does not logically imply universal validity without
an additional coverage or induction theorem.
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
Let $O\subset\mathbb N$ be finite and choose $n\notin O$.
Define $p(k)$ to be true exactly when $k\ne n$. Then all tests in
$O$ pass but $\forall k\,p(k)$ is false.\end{proof}

\chapter{Preregistered experiments and open problems}
\section{No execution is asserted}
The architecture has been mathematically specified in this manuscript;
there is no assertion that five FORGE-6 runtimes, $B^\star$, a
cross-federation bus, or an independent checker have been installed
or executed. Research must distinguish a paper specification, a
simulated protocol, a checker trace and a successful independent
reproduction.

\begin{protocol}[Minimum frozen-run record]
For each experiment record \emph{before starting}:
\begin{enumerate}
\item target $T$, definitions, complete $\Gamma_0$, environments, labels,
optional guard family and typed checker $V$ with version/hash;
\item frozen $K_0$, authorized provisional $L_t$, exact checker semantics,
trusted computing base and failure policy;
\item all five role-local FORGE-6 instances, internal policies, seeds,
$B^\star$ policy, legal service ticks, clock and spawn permissions;
\item initial bus state OFF and any authorized ON/OFF transitions,
packet schema, cross-federation gateway, and full cost accounts;
\item budgets, stop rules, frozen $\Pi_0$, revocation and pending rules,
and the six outcome categories, with
$\mathsf{UNKNOWN}$ never relabeled as $I$ or $D$;
\item preregistered baselines: legacy four-role, five-role AMLD,
passive $B^\star$, five FORGE-6 without shared routing, and full
controller with each ablation separately defined;
\item metrics: accepted settlements, complete scoped evidence,
proof size, checks, time, total charged work, memory, duplication,
missed dependencies, unauthorized promotion count, availability and
replay receipts.
\end{enumerate}
\end{protocol}

\section{Exact questions worth testing}
\begin{conjecture}[Conditional dependence yield]
On some guard-structured security families, an explicit $D$
federation will discover more certified minimal-assumption atlases
per charged resource than an otherwise matched architecture without
$D$, after accounting for its extra cost.
\end{conjecture}
\begin{conjecture}[Controlled search frontier]
On some repeated target families, policy-admissible $B^\star$
coordination improves the Pareto frontier of verified settlement,
context fidelity, nonregression and total charged work over fixed
scheduling. No unconditional claim is made.
\end{conjecture}
\begin{conjecture}[Strategic quotient discovery]
There are structured security-game families in which verifier-certified,
controller-respecting quotients reduce the number of distinct
searched strategic states enough to outweigh quotient discovery and
lifting costs.
\end{conjecture}
\begin{conjecture}[Five-federation proof-DAG reuse]
For some target distributions, cross-role reuse of identical
scope-compatible certified proof nodes exceeds all additional
communication, verification and scheduling overhead. This is the
empirical existence question suggested by Theorem~\ref{thm:reuse}.
\end{conjecture}

\section{Research boundary and conclusion}
The theorems give a larger, carefully typed structure of conditional
guarantees, not an unrestricted safety result. The system remains
vulnerable to wrong specifications, incomplete environments, erroneous
checkers, compromised execution authorities, insufficient budgets,
unfair policies, unverifiable model claims, and mistaken scope
transfers. In particular, no amount of schedule creativity proves
$T$ where the fixed theory does not support it.

The conceptual advance from \emph{AMLD Security 3} is therefore a move
from isolated, verifier-gated application sketches to a specified
\emph{investigative institution}: five complementary FORGE-6
federations search for differently typed conclusions, $D$ accounts
for assumptions, and $B^\star$ chooses legal investigative direction
without deciding mathematical truth. What this institution can
\emph{discover} is an experimental question; what it may
\emph{certify} is an explicitly formal one.

